title: Payers › Configuration feeds the rest of the app
route: /payers/:id
intro: What a payer's workflow, rules and document lists reach outside the Payers page. In the demo the working link is redrafting: updating drafts changes the matching requests on the Dashboard and sends a bell notification. The page text also says its document list is the one Reader uses on New case, and the rules feed the agents' decisions and the approval chance; the demo does not wire those, and this diagram marks them.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "A payer's workflow, rule, document list\nor payer change is saved or updated"
decision dk "Which kind of save?"
store cfg "Saved on the payer\nNew drafts use it from now on"
process nw "Page says: new drafts use it at once.\nIn the demo only the Payers page reads the saved lists back"

group gW "Wired in the demo: redrafting"
  click up "'Update N drafts' (after a payer change,\nor from the edits-waiting banner)"
  store rq "Matching requests change\nneeds a person: yes\nStatus line 'Redrafted after ... Waiting for a new signature'\nTimeline event from Scribe, Packet or Integrity"
  store nf "Bell notification 'Drafts updated'\nlinks to Case Manager"
  process dsh "Dashboard shows the new status line\nand lists the request among those needing you"
endgroup

group gC "Wired in the demo: links out of Payers"
  click oc "Click 'Open the request'\nin 'Try it on a case'"
  process od "Opens Dashboard with that request's drawer"
endgroup

group gP "Said on the page, not wired in the demo"
  process p1 "Documents tab: 'Reader uses this same list on the intake screen'\nNew case keeps its own required-document table,\nso an edited list does not change New case"
  process p2 "Rules tab: agents 'use' each rule\nNo approval chance, queue order or New case check\nreads a rule, so editing one never moves a number"
  process p3 "Header 'Approved as asked' (74% for Summit) is the figure\nNew case uses for the approval chance: it ends 14 points higher\nand starts 26 below that. It comes from decision history,\nso editing a rule or list does not move it"
  process p4 "Authorizations queue and Case Manager lists\ndo not change when drafts are redrafted"
endgroup

process prd "In the product (PRD 06)\nA rule version is stamped on every authorization;\nPacket reads the channel, form and documents; Cadence reads windows and caps;\nAdvocate reads peer-to-peer and appeal windows"

goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Requests table"
goto g2 "Continues in: Case Manager › Cases"
goto g3 "Continues in: Dashboard › Open a request"
goto g4 "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Medical records › The checklist and Continue"
goto g5 "Continues in: Authorizations › Case › Risk"
goto g7 "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Agents work › Start the run and watch it"
goto g6 "Continues in: Authorizations › Queue"

s1 --> dk
dk -->|Workflow, rule or documents| cfg --> nw
dk -->|Payer change or edits update| up --> rq --> dsh --> g1
rq --> nf --> g2
nw -.-> p1
nw -.-> p2
nw -.-> p3
nw -.-> p4
p1 --> g4
p2 --> g5
p3 --> g7
p4 --> g6
oc --> od --> g3
dk -->|Chart check| oc
p2 -.-> prd
